add('BIDEA','Opening','Hallo. This is Liam, in for Bear. The shortcut is to ask Claude for a game and submit whatever runs. Assignment one asks for something stronger: an extension whose changes you can explain and whose limits you can show. Shipping Lane is our worked example.',
 'BrutalistHesitantWriter',{'text':'A running game is\na finished assignment.','triggerWords':'finished','replacementWords':'testable','fontSize':78,'mistakeRate':0,'hesitateWithin':0,'hesitateBetween':0,'charMs':45,'jitter':0,'seed':SLUG,'brandLabel':'@NikBearBrown'},'The misconception changes from finished to testable',lead_silence_s=.8,qc={'sparse_by_design':True,'sparse_reason':'Required hesitant writer; the visible correction frames the lesson.'})
add('BDEFS','Opening','Five terms. A starter is the existing game you extend. A collider is the boundary physics uses. A regression check tests behavior that must survive a change. A fixture is a controlled test setup, not a human playtest. A revision identifies the exact source being demonstrated.',
 'ClaudeDefinitions',{'title':'Terms In This Lecture','terms':[{'term':'starter','meaning':'the existing game you extend'},{'term':'collider','meaning':'the boundary physics uses'},{'term':'regression','meaning':'check behavior that must survive an edit'},{'term':'fixture','meaning':'controlled test setup, not human play'},{'term':'revision','meaning':'the exact source being demonstrated'}],'folderLabel':'@NikBearBrown'},'Five prerequisites, in teaching order',qc={'sparse_by_design':True,'sparse_reason':'Required key terms; prerequisite vocabulary, not a body slide.'})

A='I · Predict Before You Build'
pipe('B01',A,'Predict, Build, Inspect, Revise','Here is the working loop. Write the brief, make one bounded change, run the game, inspect what happened, and revise from that evidence. Walker is a set of instructions and tools for following that loop. It does not replace your judgment.',['Brief','Change','Play','Inspect','Revise'],['document','adapter','monitor','scanner','document'],'Conceptual Walker loop · assignment §1–3')
table('B02',A,'Two Required Changes','Your task starts with Walker Jumpman, not an empty project. Change the character meaningfully and add at least two jump landings beyond the original route. Move the finish. Shipping Lane goes further, but blocks, bugs and power-ups are example choices, not extra assignment requirements.',[['Character','Distinct silhouette'],['Level','Two new jump landings'],['Finish','Beyond the extension'],['Blocks / bugs','Optional example scope']],'Assignment 1 · Your task / Build It')
table('B03',A,'Work In Your Own Copy','Use your own copy or a course-authorized repository, with a name beginning walker dash. Credit the starter. Import its project file in Godot rather than creating an empty project. Use your course Claude Code access; paid assets and purchased credits are not required.',[['Project','walker- prefix'],['Source','Your authorized copy'],['Open','godot/project.godot'],['Cost','No paid assets required']],'Assignment 1 · Your task; existing project.godot')
table('B04',A,'Write The Change Brief','Before edits, write your character concept, the new player decision, the behavior to preserve, and at least two failures with checks. Keep those first predictions. The Shipping Lane brief predicted hidden camera or label problems and a raised landing that the unchanged jump might not clear.',[['Concept','Clawd silhouette'],['Decision','New jump landings'],['Preserve','Jump / controls / retry'],['Predict','Geometry and camera failures']],'CHANGE-BRIEF.md · 2026-10-09 addition')
table('B05',A,'Ask For A Plan, Not A Miracle','Ask Claude to read the README, build report and change brief, then locate drawing, collider, level data, camera, finish and tests. Require a plan before editing. The assignment supplies that prompt; it is not a shell command. Accept one step, inspect its diff, and run its relevant checks.',[['Read','README + brief + report'],['Locate','Art / collider / level'],['Plan','No edits yet'],['Step','Diff + check + limits']],'Assignment 1 · Work in inspectable increments')
table('B06',A,'Keep A Baseline','Run and play the starter before changing it. Save the engine version, source revision and results. This example retained twenty-five mechanics checks and nine keyboard checks. Those checks establish a baseline for their cases, not that every player will understand the route.',[['Mechanics','25 checks retained'],['Keyboard','9 checks retained'],['Identity','Engine + source revision'],['Human baseline','Play it yourself']],'TEST-REPORT.md · Original mechanics / keyboard; assignment §3')

A='II · Change The Character, Keep The Contract'
code('B07',A,'Drawing Is Not Physics','Inspect the starter drawing before choosing an art pipeline. This version routes drawing into Clawd Art. Its broad body, arms, eyes and legs make it recognizable, not merely recolored. The movement function remains separate. A new drawing does not automatically define a new physics body.', 'func _draw() -> void:\n    ClawdArt.paint(self, animation_name,\n        animation_seconds, Vector2.ZERO,\n        0.32, facing, animation_name == "jump")','player.gd · _draw(); whitespace reflow only')
code('B08',A,'Keep The Collision Boundary','The existing collider is eighteen by twenty-eight game units, centered fourteen units above the origin. Preserve it for the initial art change. Clawd’s arms extend beyond it, so a visible overlap might not mean contact. Inspect that trade-off while facing both ways and while jumping.', 'var shape := RectangleShape2D.new()\nshape.size = Vector2(18, 28)\nvar collider := CollisionShape2D.new()\ncollider.shape = shape\ncollider.position = Vector2(0, -14)\nadd_child(collider)','player.gd · _ready(); exact expressions')
table('B09',A,'States Must Read At Game Size','Check standing, walking, facing left and right, jumping, failure and completion in the actual game. The separate eighteen-animation gallery is diagnostic, not eighteen abilities. The airborne pose is held so the art does not add a second decorative jump on top of the physical trajectory.',[['Facing','Left and right'],['Airborne','Held pose; one trajectory'],['Failure / finish','Distinct visible states'],['Gallery','Diagnostic, not abilities']],'player.gd · visual_animation / _draw; README.md')
table('B10',A,'Keep The Original Jump','Record what must survive. This example keeps speed, jump velocity, gravity and the collision body. If a new landing is impossible, revise the geometry first. Do not remove collision checks or increase jump strength simply to turn a failed route into a passing report.',[['Speed','160'],['Jump velocity','−320'],['Gravity','960'],['Collider','18 × 28']],'CHANGE-BRIEF.md · Shipping Lane preservation; tuning.gd')

A='III · Extend The Route, Not Just The Floor'
table('B11',A,'From First Steps To Shipping Lane','Read First Steps and its session code together. Shipping Lane keeps the original route and appends new decisions beyond it. Width grows from nine hundred sixty to three thousand two hundred units, and the finish moves to thirty-one hundred twelve. These are this example’s values, not a prescribed student layout.',[['Original width','960'],['New width','3,200'],['New finish x','3,112'],['Extra gaps','Four']],'first_steps.json / shipping_lane.json · example values')
code('B12',A,'Two New Landing Islands','These two platform entries give the first required new landings. The arrays are horizontal position, vertical position, width and height. Their placement makes a real gap, not a cosmetic floor extension. The route check later verifies actual landings using normal input, rather than assuming coordinates prove reachability.', '[1312, 320, 272, 64],\n[1648, 320, 416, 64]','shipping_lane.json · solids excerpt; formatting condensed')
table('B13',A,'Add A Player Decision','Ask what the player must decide. Here, crossing a gap and reading a patrol bug happen in the new section; a raised route offers optional tokens. Your assignment can stay smaller. Two meaningful reachable landings beat a long empty corridor or a collection of untested features.',[['Required route','New landings'],['Encounter','Read a patrol bug'],['Raised route','Optional reward'],['Student scope','May be simpler']],'Shipping Lane GDD / assignment §2')
code('B14',A,'Camera Follows The New Bounds','Now follow the dependencies. The camera clamps against level width, so its right boundary moves with the extension. Backgrounds, labels, hazard art and the finish must agree with the data too. Inspect the next landing before jumping; a physically reachable platform can still be hidden from the player.', 'camera.position.x = clampf(\n    player.position.x + 100,\n    320, float(level.width) - 320)','session.gd · camera clamp; whitespace reflow only')
code('B15',A,'Progress Must Follow The Finish','The interface needs the same repair. This version computes progress from spawn to the current finish rather than keeping the old fixed distance. Moving only the flag can leave a bar that promises completion too early. Check the source expression against the visible bar on the extended route.', 'var progress: float = clampf(\n    (game.player.position.x - float(game.level.spawn[0]))\n    / (float(game.level.finish[0])\n    - float(game.level.spawn[0])), 0, 1)','hud.gd · progress; whitespace reflow only')
table('B16',A,'A Failed Jump Chooses The Edit','One real attempt stalled at horizontal position twenty-two thirty. A reward block obstructed the raised-lane approach. The revision moved block Q zero five three cells left, from cell one thirty-eight to one thirty-five. Jump strength and collider stayed unchanged. Keep that failed attempt beside the fix.',[['Observed','Jump blocked at x=2230'],['Before','Q05 cell (138, 16)'],['After','Q05 cell (135, 16)'],['Preserved','Jump and collider']],'FRICTIONAL.md · actual 2026-10-09 route revision')
table('B17',A,'Inspect What The Engine Actually Draws','A second inspection found missing question marks and brick markings. The tile layer painted over its own drawing callback. The fix put those marks in the tile atlas. A passing mechanics check had not established visual clarity; actual engine frames revealed the problem.',[['Expected','Visible block markings'],['Observed','Marks hidden'],['Cause','Tile layer drawing order'],['Fix','Marks in tile atlas']],'terrain.gd · atlas; FRICTIONAL.md · native pilot revision')
code('B18',A,'Optional Rule: State Before Reward','The example also adds blocks. This source marks a block used before changing its tile or emitting the reward, so repeated head contact cannot pay twice. A powered brick follows the removal branch. This is optional scope; the next shot shows the actual consequence, not a simulated success.', 'blocks[cell].used = true\nif kind == "brick":\n    erase_cell(cell)\nelse:\n    set_cell(cell, 0, Vector2i(4, 0))\n    reward.emit(kind,\n        Vector2(cell * 16) + Vector2(8, 0))','terrain.gd · bump(); whitespace reflow only')
